### Health
GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/health

### Create log source
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/log-sources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Firewall Gateway",
  "source_type": "firewall",
  "host": "fw-lab.local",
  "environment": "staging",
  "status": "active"
}

### Ingest security event
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/security-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source_id": 1,
  "event_type": "authentication_failure",
  "severity": "high",
  "source_ip": "192.0.2.55",
  "destination_ip": "192.0.2.10",
  "username": "lab-user",
  "message": "Synthetic repeated failed login event"
}

### Create detection rule
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/detection-rules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Failed Login Detection",
  "description": "Detect repeated failed authentication events in training data.",
  "event_type": "authentication_failure",
  "severity_threshold": "high",
  "is_enabled": true
}

### Create alert (use event_id and rule_id returned above)
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/alerts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_id": 1,
  "rule_id": 1,
  "title": "Possible brute-force activity",
  "severity": "high"
}

### Create investigation
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/investigations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "alert_id": 1,
  "analyst_name": "SOC Analyst",
  "findings": "Review of synthetic authentication events.",
  "action_taken": "Escalated for simulated review"
}

### Search, filter, pagination
GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/security-events?search=failed&severity=high&page=1&per_page=10

### Validation error example (expected 422)
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/log-sources
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Missing fields"}
